  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Federal contract obligations for NAICS 541715 (Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences) total $27.7B in FY2026 to date. There are 13,412 awards with an average award size of $2.1M. Obligations fell 40.3% year over year. Recent fiscal-year history shows a peak at $46.3B in FY25 and then $27.7B in FY26. The Department of Defense is the largest buyer at $18B, followed by NASA at $4B and the Department of Energy at $3.4B. Other buying agencies with measurable obligations include GSA ($990M), HHS ($827M), DHS ($98.9M), Commerce ($79.9M), DOT ($64.9M), Interior ($55.7M), and Justice ($31.2M). Leading vendors in FY2026 to date include FLUOR MARINE PROPULSION, LLC ($4B), CALIFORNIA INSTITUTE OF TECHNOLOGY ($1.7B), and THE JOHNS HOPKINS UNIVERSITY APPLIED PHYSICS LABORATORY LLC ($1.2B). Multiple Lockheed Martin entries appear among top vendors with $971M, $911M, and $715M awards. These figures are contract obligations and current-year totals are partial (fiscal year to date).",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has spending trended recently?",
        "body": "Obligations rose from $29B in FY21 to $46.3B in FY25 before falling to $27.7B in FY26. Obligations fell 40.3% year over year into FY26. That decline follows four straight years of growth from FY21 through FY25. The FY26 total is a partial, fiscal year to date figure."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who concentrates the buying and award dollars?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense accounts for the largest share at $18B in FY2026 to date. NASA ($4B) and the Department of Energy ($3.4B) are the next largest buyers, with several other agencies reporting under $1B. On the vendor side, FLUOR MARINE PROPULSION, LLC leads at $4B, followed by CALIFORNIA INSTITUTE OF TECHNOLOGY ($1.7B) and THE JOHNS HOPKINS UNIVERSITY APPLIED PHYSICS LABORATORY LLC ($1.2B). Multiple Lockheed Martin entries show sizable obligations spread across $971M, $911M, and $715M."
      }
    ]
  },
